    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d749">

                <pb facs="0776" n="518" xml:id="pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857Ar1/21</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Cork</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Queenstown</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1915-08-22T09:00:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1915-08-21T00:00:00-00:25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received August
                            22, 1915, 9 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Have failed in devoutest efforts to discover any evidence that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi> was warned by submarine or convoyed by war
                    vessel. She did not attempt to ram submarine nor go to assistance of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dunsley</hi>. It is barely possible, however, that other
                    facts may yet be found.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
